| `dynamic_analysis_unsafe` | MUST | yes | no | **N/A**: {% if stack == 'dotnet' %}C# is memory-safe; it applies only to `unsafe` code{% else %}it applies only to code in a memory-unsafe language, such as C or C++{% endif %}. |

## Gold

The [gold criteria](https://www.bestpractices.dev/en/criteria/2), 23 in all.

### Basics

| Criterion | Req | N/A | URL | Answer and evidence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `achieve_silver` | MUST | no | no | **Check**: the site sets it once the silver level is earned. |
| `bus_factor` | MUST | no | yes | **Person**: two or more people who could carry the project on; Unmet with one maintainer, which keeps gold from being earned. |
| `contributors_unassociated` | MUST | no | yes | **Person**: at least two significant contributors from different organizations. |
| `copyright_per_file` | MUST | no | no | {% if csharp %}**Check**: the C# file header `.editorconfig` sets starts with the copyright line, and the build fails a C# file without it; check every other source file, such as scripts.{% else %}**Gap**: Unmet until each source file starts with a copyright line.{% endif %} |
| `license_per_file` | MUST | no | no | {% if csharp and spdx %}**Check**: the C# file header holds `SPDX-License-Identifier: {{ spdx }}`, and the build fails a C# file without it; check every other source file.{% else %}**Gap**: Unmet until each source file has an `SPDX-License-Identifier` line.{% endif %} |

### Change Control

| Criterion | Req | N/A | URL | Answer and evidence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `repo_distributed` | MUST | no | no | **Met**: Git; autofill. |
| `small_tasks` | MUST | no | yes | **Check**: Met while open issues carry the `good first issue` label that [CONTRIBUTING.md](../CONTRIBUTING.md) names{% if not github %}; create the label first{% endif %}. |
| `require_2FA` | MUST | no | no | **Person**: the {{ host }} {% if github %}organization{% else %}group{% endif %} requires two-factor authentication; only an owner can set and confirm it. |
| `secure_2FA` | SHOULD | no | no | **Person**: {% if github %}the organization allows only secure two-factor methods{% else %}members use a security key or an authenticator app, never SMS{% endif %}. |

### Quality

| Criterion | Req | N/A | URL | Answer and evidence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `code_review_standards` | MUST | yes | yes | **Met**: [CONTRIBUTING.md](../CONTRIBUTING.md), Review Requirements. |
| `two_person_review` | MUST | no | no | **Person**: at least half of the changes reviewed before release by someone other than their author; Unmet with one maintainer{% if review %}, as NCode Review's approval is a bot's{% endif %}. |
| `build_reproducible` | MUST | yes | yes | {% if stack == 'dotnet' %}**Check**: deterministic builds{% if library %} with Source Link{% endif %}; Met once a rebuild of a release's tag is shown to match it.{% else %}**Check**: N/A when no build occurs; otherwise Met once a rebuild of a release's tag is shown to match it.{% endif %} |
| `test_invocation` | MUST | no | yes | {% if test_command %}**Met**: `{{ test_command }}`, in [CONTRIBUTING.md](../CONTRIBUTING.md), Build and Test.{% else %}**Gap**: the project has no test command yet.{% endif %} |
| `test_continuous_integration` | MUST | no | yes | **Met**: `{{ ci }}` runs the build and the tests on every {{ pr }}. |
